# Dev-profile (overflow-checks ON) decode sweep of the full dav1d corpus
# ======================================================================
# Why: releases <= 0.5.7 crashed a DEBUG-profile consumer with
#   looprestoration_arm.rs:465:30 "attempt to multiply with overflow"
# on 8-bit/issues/320_tennis.ivf. Column 30 of that line is
# `row_start * REST_UNIT_STRIDE`, where
# `let row_start = (row_offset as isize - 1) as usize` is usize::MAX at
# row_offset == 0 -- an INDEX multiply, not the `a * n - b * b` below it. With
# overflow-checks OFF it wraps to the intended offset, so the failure exists
# only in the dev profile, and no test in this repo had ever decoded a
# bitstream in that profile (every decode suite opened with
# `#[cfg(debug_assertions)] compile_error!`).
#
# This sweep is the empirical half of the fix: it establishes that on `main`
# the whole corpus decodes in the dev profile with zero overflow traps, and
# that the new `sgr_ab_{8,16}bpc` box-sum range assertions hold on real data.
#
# commit         : b2d76b7 (docs+test(looprestoration_arm): state the sgr
#                           box-sum range invariant ...)
# date           : 2026-08-31
# host           : aarch64-apple-darwin (Darwin 25.5.0, Apple Silicon)
# profile        : dev  (opt-level 0, debug-assertions ON, overflow-checks ON)
# features       : --no-default-features --features bitdepth_8,bitdepth_16
# binary         : target/debug/examples/decode_md5
# invocation     : decode_md5 -q --threads 4 <vector>   (per vector, serial)
# corpus         : test-vectors/dav1d-test-data, every *.ivf + *.obu
#
# RESULTS
# -------
# vectors run              : 783   (8-bit, 10-bit, 12-bit, multi-bit/argon)
# nonzero exit / panic     : 0
# assertion failures       : 0     (sgr_ab_8bpc / sgr_ab_16bpc range checks)
# overflow traps           : 0
# wall time                : ~20 min total, run in 4 chunks
#
# The same sweep was run BEFORE the assertions were added (same commit base,
# same corpus, 783/783 clean), so the assertions add no failures of their own.
#
# LR variant coverage, from `--features __lrvarcov` on the committed vectors:
#   8bpc : wiener5, sgr_3x3, sgr_5x5, sgr_mix
#   16bpc: sgr_3x3, sgr_5x5, sgr_mix
#   (8-bit/issues/320_tennis.ivf -- the vector in the crash report -- reports
#    `LRVAR 8bpc sgr_mix` and `LRVAR 8bpc wiener5`, so it does reach the
#    kernel that panicked on 0.5.7.)
#
# MUTATION CHECK (the guard actually fires)
# -----------------------------------------
# Reintroducing the 0.5.7 aa_base arithmetic in `sgr_ab_8bpc`, in a form whose
# WRAPPED value is byte-identical to `(row + 1) * S + 2`:
#     let row_start = (row as isize - 1) as usize;
#     let base = (2 * S + 3).wrapping_add(row_start * S)
#                           .wrapping_sub(S).wrapping_add(S - 1);
#   dev     : 3 of 4 `decode_md5_committed` tests FAIL,
#             "attempt to multiply with overflow" at looprestoration_arm.rs:875:27
#   release : 4 of 4 PASS, every committed MD5 byte-identical
# That asymmetry is the defect this campaign closed.
#
# DEV-PROFILE SUITE COST (why the release-only gates were removed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# decode_md5_committed   4 tests   0.75 s
# safe_simd_crashes     15 tests   0.29 s
# fuzz_regression        3 tests   5.12 s   (33 seeds x 5 entry points)
# For contrast, the downloaded dav1d corpus above is ~20 min in the dev
# profile -- THAT is what "debug decode is too slow" was true of. It was never
# true of the committed stills.
